{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792833154,"nonce":"BbYWmXsypOhovcUnnckFW28M+FE=","title":"Compiler: a typed cast from bool to a float type lowers to a bitcast","message":"`TypedExpression::Cast { expr: \u003cbool\u003e, target_type: F64 }` lowers through `select_cast_op` in ssa.rs, which has a Bool arm only for integer targets (ZExt). Bool to F32/F64 falls through to Bitcast, so `true` becomes the f64 with bit pattern 1 (5e-324) on the interpreter, Cranelift and LLVM tiers alike.\n\nReproducer: a TypeScript frontend emitting `Cast(bool -\u003e F64)` for `+t` with `const t = true; console.log(+t)` prints 5e-324 on every tier (expected 1). The TypeScript frontend now casts bool -\u003e I32 -\u003e F64, which selects ZExt then SiToFp and prints 1, so this does not block TS work.\n\nExpected: Bool -\u003e float selects an unsigned int-to-float conversion (UiToFp or ZExt then SiToFp), matching the Bool -\u003e int ZExt arm.","files":null}]}